    "created_at": "2025-08-05T15:07:34Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-08-05T15:07:34Z",
    "body": "Some spec changes which I think will be needed to support this use case based on my prototyping so far:\n- The select’s [list of options](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/form-elements.html#concept-select-option-list) needs to do a flat tree traversal to look for option elements instead of a regular DOM traversal.\n- The option HTML element insertion steps and HTML element removal steps need to do a flat tree ancestor traversal instead of a regular DOM ancestor traversal.\n  - This runs the [selectedness setting algorithm](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/form-elements.html#selectedness-setting-algorithm), which needs to be run every time an option is added or removed from a select.\n- When slot assignment is recalculated and a [slot change is signaled](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#signal-a-slot-change), any ancestor select element of the slot element should run its selectedness setting algorithm to account for options which may have been added or removed.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
