    "updated_at": "2025-08-05T16:07:56Z",
    "body": "IMO, this is a necessary change and while I understand we are in \"feature\" land at this point due to this requiring spec changes, this was clearly a \"miss\" in the spec process itself. It's incredibly common for design systems to be built nowadays using Web Components. As it stands with the current implementation, usage within the shadow DOM is not feasible at all, meaning that this improvement to the platform cannot be used with the platform's actual component model. We do not have a method of extending this element as a built-in, nor do we have a way to attach a shadow. Without this improvement, custom element authors who wish to provide a declarative \"select\" that benefits from Web Components as a technology must rebuild everything, using heavy-handed JS, custom DOM and templating, and provide their own a11y support. That's been par for the course, but it is exactly the reason that myself and others who have authored custom element libraries were active early on in Open UI. We'd like to stop rebuilding this and we'd like to be able to use web-native technologies rather than large JS frameworks to do so 😄.\n\nPlease consider prioritizing the changes to the spec so that we can make use of this improvement to the platform!",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
