    "body": "To me this seems like an obvious bugfix, why is it even discussed as a feature, asking authors to justify why they want to do this and when? *Any* child element should be specifiable _either_ directly, _or_ via slots. That’s what slots _do_. The only reason we may not want to fix it is web compat, or if it's tremendously difficult to implement. Then, it's basically a wontfix bug, not a feature that didn't get implemented.",
