    "body": "> > Worth bearing in mind that people might also want to slot a button into their select. I don't see anyone mentioning that so far and that would presumably also require a bit of heavy lifting.\n> \n> I think we do need to be more careful here. My understanding is that putting a button within a select right now is considered invalid and is somehow ignored. We may want to apply similar constraints when we're looking at the slotted options.\n\nI agree with Luke's concern, this will be hard to implement. The first child button element of the select element is slotted into the button slot for base appearance, replaces the default/fallback rendering of the button, and is valid per the content model.",
