    "created_at": "2026-09-17T20:38:57Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-09-17T20:41:53Z",
    "body": "> In general none of HTML's elements currently support this. E.g., this doesn't work for `table`. I'm not convinced (yet) that solving this in isolation for `select` is a good idea.\n\nYeah it would be sweet if for all native elements that read children, if they were all updates to read flat tree children.\n\nCould it a be a breaking change for any systems already written on current native elements? If so, maybe make it opt in with a new global attribute:\n\n```html\n<!-- inside shadow root -->\n<select readflat>\n  <slot></slot>\n</slot>\n```\n\nOr something. And it would also enable this:\n\n```html\n<select readflat>\n  <template shadowrootmode=\"open\">\n    ... options here ...\n  </template>\n</slot>\n```\n\nThe element with readflat would just read flat children, it wouldn't matter if children are from a slot or from top level of a shadow root.\n\nIdeally readflat wouldn't be needed, I only gave the idea in case back compat will be needed. Ideally elements should always act on flat children because that's what people expect from composition.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
